### 17. Number of Islands — LeetCode #200

**Pattern:** DFS / Graph

```java
class Solution {
    public int numIslands(char[][] grid) {

        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {

            for (int j = 0; j < grid[0].length; j++) {

                if (grid[i][j] == '1') {

                    count++;

                    dfs(grid, i, j);
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }

    public void dfs(char[][] grid, int row, int col) {

        if (row < 0 || row >= grid.length ||
            col < 0 || col >= grid[0].length ||
            grid[row][col] == '0') {

            return;
        }

        grid[row][col] = '0';

        dfs(grid, row + 1, col);
        dfs(grid, row - 1, col);
        dfs(grid, row, col + 1);
        dfs(grid, row, col - 1);
    }
}
```

**Example:**

```text
Input:

1 1 0 0
1 0 0 1
0 0 1 1

Output: 3
```

When we find `'1'`, one island found.

Then DFS visits the **entire connected island** and changes it to `0`.

**Remember:**

```text
↑
↓
←
→
```

Only four directions.

**Time:** `O(rows × columns)`
**Space:** `O(rows × columns)` worst-case recursion.

