### 18. Search in Rotated Sorted Array — LeetCode #33

**Pattern:** Modified Binary Search

```java
class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {

        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {

            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            }

            // Left half is sorted
            if (nums[left] <= nums[mid]) {

                if (nums[left] <= target && target < nums[mid]) {
                    right = mid - 1;
                } else {
                    left = mid + 1;
                }

            }

            // Right half is sorted
            else {

                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[right]) {
                    left = mid + 1;
                } else {
                    right = mid - 1;
                }
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
}
```

**Example:**

```text
Input:
nums = [4,5,6,7,0,1,2]
target = 0

Output:
4
```

### 🧠 Main trick

Normal binary search-la sorted array full-aa irukkum.

Here:

```text
[4,5,6,7,0,1,2]
       ↑
    rotation
```

Every iteration-la **at least one half is sorted**.

```text
Left half sorted?
    ↓
Does target exist there?
    ↓
Yes → search left
No  → search right
```

**Time:** `O(log n)`
**Space:** `O(1)`

